const GLOSSARY=[
['Niche','A focused audience with a shared interest. The narrower the niche, the easier it is to stand out and sell.'],
['Hook','The first three seconds of a video or the first line of a post. Its only job is to stop the scroll.'],
['Conversion','The moment someone does the thing you wanted — buys, signs up, or leaves their details.'],
['CTR','The share of people who saw your ad and clicked it. Below 1% usually means the ad is not interesting enough.'],
['ROAS','Return on ad spend. ROAS 3 means $3 came back for every $1 spent.'],
['CPM','Cost to show an ad to a thousand people. Useful for comparing platforms.'],
['Margin','What is left after all costs. Not what the customer paid — what stays with you.'],
['AOV','Average order value: what a typical customer spends in one purchase. Raising it is the cheapest way to earn more.'],
['Pixel','Tracking code on your site that tells the ad platform who did what. Without it, advertising is blind.'],
['Leads','People who showed interest and left details, but have not bought yet.'],
['Organic vs paid','Organic is reach you did not pay for. Paid is reach you bought. A healthy business uses both.'],
['UGC','User-generated content — looks real, so it converts better than polished ads.'],
['Monetisation','Turning an audience or content into income: sponsorships, products, affiliates or memberships.'],
['Retainer','A fixed monthly fee for ongoing work. The basis of stable freelance and social income.'],
['MRR','Monthly recurring revenue — the number that matters most for apps and subscriptions.'],
['CTA','Call to action — the line that asks the viewer to do one clear thing.']];

