const LEGAL=[
{t:'Minors and contracts',d:'In most countries a contract signed by someone under 18 can be voided, and legally significant actions need a parent or guardian\'s consent. In practice: payment processing, supplier agreements and client contracts should be in a parent\'s name. Small everyday purchases typical for your age do not need special approval.'},
{t:'Business registration and tax',d:'Business registration and tax numbers require an adult account holder. Until 18, the standard route is a parent registering and formally operating the business while you run it day to day. Income from a business is taxable and reportable, even when it is small. Before there is steady income, talk to an accountant or your local tax authority once.'},
{t:'Copyright and trademarks',d:'Never use images, music, video, logos or characters that are not yours — not "just in a story", not even with credit. In print on demand this is the single most common reason accounts get closed and legal letters arrive. Use properly licensed libraries, platform-native music, or work you made yourself.'},
{t:'Advertising disclosure',d:'When you are paid, given a free product, or earning a commission for a recommendation, you must disclose it clearly ("paid partnership", "affiliate link"). Hiding it counts as misleading advertising in most jurisdictions. It also pays off: an audience that finds out on its own stops trusting you.'},
{t:'Consumer rights and refunds',d:'Distance selling to consumers comes with a legal right of cancellation in many countries, within defined timeframes. Your store must show accurate product details, total price, delivery times and a clear refund policy. Do not copy a policy from another site — write one that matches what you actually offer.'},
{t:'Customer privacy and data',d:'Names, phone numbers, addresses and emails are personal data with legal protection. Collect only what you need, never share it, and never send marketing without explicit prior consent. Anywhere you collect data, you need a privacy policy. Stricter rules apply if your users are children.'},
{t:'Payments and safety',d:'Take payments only through recognised processors, never a personal transfer from someone you do not know. Never send identity documents, home address or passwords to a "supplier" or a "mentor". A guaranteed-income promise in exchange for an upfront payment is a reliable sign of a scam.'},
{t:'What this is not',d:'Everything here is general explanation, not legal, tax or financial advice. Before any decision with real financial consequences, talk to a parent, and where it matters, to a lawyer or an accountant.'}];

